# Rust build artifacts
/target
**/target/
**/*.rs.bk
Cargo.lock.bak

# Lockfile: not checked in for libraries,
# handled in a separate workflow step for binaries (tools/*).
# Decision: a workspace with bindings and tools -> commit Cargo.lock.
# Cargo.lock

# IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*.swo
.DS_Store

# Secrets / Local Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.pem
*.key
!tests/fixtures/**/*.pem
!tests/fixtures/**/*.key
!**/tests/fixtures/**/*.pem
!**/tests/fixtures/**/*.key

# github/ is a curated mirror (its own sub-repository with its own .git),
# filled by hand from the root state. Do NOT track it from the root
# repository — otherwise it is versioned twice.
/github/

# LLVM coverage instrumentation output (besides the *.profraw/profdata already covered)
/target/llvm-cov-target
/target/nextest

# Coverage
*.profraw
*.profdata
/coverage

# Fuzzing
/fuzz/target
/fuzz/corpus
/fuzz/artifacts

# Benchmarks
/target/criterion

# Python artifacts (for dds-py wheel builds)
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.egg-info/
.pytest_cache/

# C# / .NET artifacts
# (bin/obj only in the actual .NET project directories, not
# globally — otherwise Rust binary modules under crates/*/src/bin/ are
# ignored too. Pragmatic scope: the dds-cs crate and the Tauri dashboard.)
crates/cs/**/bin/
crates/cs/**/obj/
tools/dashboard/**/bin/
tools/dashboard/**/obj/
*.user

# Java artifacts
*.class
/target-java
crates/java-omgdds/java/target/

# Node/Tauri artifacts (dds-dashboard)
node_modules/
/tools/dashboard/src-tauri/target
/tools/dashboard/dist

# Documentation builds
/documentation/_build
/documentation/.venv

# LaTeX spec builds (do not commit the build output under
# dds-*-1.0/main.pdf; releases/ on the other hand is tracked for phase F).
/documentation/specs/dds-amqp-1.0/main.pdf
/documentation/specs/dds-ts-1.0/main.pdf
/documentation/specs/**/main.aux
/documentation/specs/**/main.log
/documentation/specs/**/main.out
/documentation/specs/**/main.toc
/documentation/specs/**/main.synctex.gz
/documentation/specs/**/build/

# Standards cache — produced locally by internal/standards/fetch.sh,
# not tracked in the repository for IP/copyright reasons (see internal/standards/README.md)
/internal/standards/cache/*
!/internal/standards/cache/.gitkeep
interop-artifacts/

# cargo-mutants output (regenerated per run, very large)
/mutants-out
mutants.out/

# Local test concept document (input only, not versioned)
tests.docx

# Maturin/PyO3 compiled Python module (built by 'maturin develop')
crates/py/python/zerodds/_core*.so
crates/py/python/zerodds/_core*.dylib

# Playwright MCP cache
.playwright-mcp/

# Publish-run artifacts (manually generated, run-specific). scripts/publish-crates.sh
# writes .publish-<version>.{order,log}; the broad glob covers every version slug.
.publish-*
.dryrun-*

# The public example mirror (zerodds-examples / "zero-dds-snippets") is its own
# git repository checked out inside this tree — never track it from the root.
/zerodds-examples/
endpoints/**/build/
endpoints/**/bin/
endpoints/**/obj/
endpoints/**/*.class
endpoints/**/_build/

# The TypeScript runtime's build output. `run-tests.sh` makes both, and
# `typescript_reader_generates.rs` writes the third: a generated reader
# per shape, type-checked in place and kept only until the next run.
runtime/typescript/dist/
runtime/typescript/dist-tests/
runtime/typescript/dist-generated/

# The Ada runtime's build output. `gprbuild -P runtime/ada/zd_wire.gpr`
# writes objects, ALI files, the binder's generated unit and the
# self-test binary into the project's own object directory.
runtime/ada/obj/

# Build artefacts inside matrix cells: the kept src/ trees carry the
# GENERATED SOURCES as the record; compiled binaries beside them are
# reproducible ballast (2294 copies of ZeroDds.Wire.dll before this).
# The measurement tree moved to the `zerodds-matrix` repository on
# 2026-08-26 and is cloned into `matrix/` here; see
# docs/matrix-repo-split.md for why. The rules below stay for the
# history and for anyone with an older checkout.
/matrix/
matrix/**/*.dll
matrix/**/*.pdb
matrix/**/src/**/*.js
matrix/**/src/**/*.js.map
matrix/**/src/**/obj/
matrix/**/src/**/bin/

# The interop gate's vendor clients are built in place. `tests/interop/ci/rti/`
# additionally holds what `rtiddsgen` emits — RTI's own generated sources,
# which are licensed to this installation and must not travel with the tree.
tests/interop/ci/fastdds/build/
tests/interop/ci/rti/build/

# Zig's build cache. It landed in `53ab8c5ba69` through a `git add`
# on the whole directory — 43 files, linker output among them. A build
# cache in the repository also breaks a checkout on any host that has
# its own, which is how it was found.
.zig-cache/

# `zig build`'s install prefix. `endpoints/**/bin/` above already catches
# `zig-out/bin/`, which is where the example lands today — but that is the
# install layout and not a rule about it: a build step that installs a
# header, a library or a linker map puts it in `zig-out/lib`, `zig-out/include`
# or next to the binary, and none of those are covered.
zig-out/

# Local runtime artifacts, not part of the tree.
erl_crash.dump
runtime/csharp/bin/
runtime/csharp/obj/

# coverage-as-by-product (ci/zd-test.sh): instrumented target dir + per-job evidence
/target-cov
**/target-cov/
/ci-evidence
